# THE SIFREI ROWS on Numbers 8:1-26 and 10:1-12:16 (THE NUMBERS WALK sitting 3 — BEHA'ALOTCHA, 2026-09-10): piskaot 59-63 and 72-106
# by POSITION, 51 rows at the shelf's row grain, each opened and verdicted; the middah named where the row argues by one
# (logic/MIDDOT.md: I1 a-fortiori, I2 the identity of wording, I3 the paradigm, I4 general-particular, I13 two verses reconciled by a
# third; E-codes for the narrative rules). Four heads placed by position (59 headless = 8:2; 62 "3:24" = 8:24, CREDITED to
# num_04_kehat's ledger; 80 "10:30" = 10:31; 102 "Ibid. 4" = 12:4) — asserted in beha_ink.py. Piska 62 is CREDITED, not re-read.
from beha_ink import *
S = {}
def srow(p, r, verdict, prose): S[(p, r)] = (verdict, prose)

# ---- piskaot 59-63 (8:2-4, 8:24-26): the lamps, the menorah's making, the Levites' ages ----
srow(59, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'THE LAMPS FACE THE MIDDLE (the row on 8:2 — the head unparsed in the export, placed by position between 58 on 7:89 and 60 on 8:3). "Toward the face of the lampstand shall the seven lamps light" against Exod 25:37\'s "to light across its face": the six lamps turn toward the central shaft — three north, three south, one in the middle — whence R. Nathan: THE MIDDLE ONE IS HONORED (the exam\'s Menachot 98b; Shabbat 22b). "Speak to Aaron" — the section is Aaron\'s, the words to him; "when you raise the lamps" — MAKE STEPS for it (the ascent before the lampstand); "do they light forever?" — Lev 24:3 "from evening to morning"; and the one that burns continually (Lev 24:2) is THE WESTERN LAMP, from which the rest are kindled toward evening. The lamps\' geometry as a rule read off "toward the face" (the phrase\'s two seats, 8:2-3 — computed).')
srow(60, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'AARON DID NOT CHANGE; THE SONS EQUATED WITH THE FATHER BY THE THREE-FACET PARADIGM. "And Aaron did so" — his praise: as Moses told him, without change ("he did so" for Aaron, the clause\'s one seat — computed); "he raised its lamps" — the three-step ascent the priest stood on, the oil jug left on the second step; "as the LORD commanded" — HALF A LOG per lamp (the measure the data channel carries); the sons equated with the father for the lampstand from Lev 24:3 "Aaron and his sons"; for the INCENSE by induction (I3): "service in the tent of meeting" alone is refuted by Yom Kippur (linen, not gold); "in golden vestments" too is refuted by the anointed priest\'s bull (not "continually"); "I learn a thing from a thing similar in THREE ways — tent, gold, continually — not in one or two": the three-facet paradigm stated a second time (Naso\'s 6:1 the first — MIDDOT.md), the refutations answered by the count.')
srow(61, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'BEATEN FROM THE BAR — WHAT IS VALID FOR THE LAMPSTAND IS INVALID FOR THE TRUMPETS. R. Yishmael: the lampstand one of THREE THINGS Moses could not visualize until shown "with the finger" (the new moon Exod 12:2; the unclean creatures Lev 11:29); מִקְשָׁה ("beaten work") read as an acronym, "from the hard [bar]" (E30 notarikon); its bowls, knobs and flowers from the one bar (Exod 25:31, 25:36 "from it"); "beaten" RESTATED to invalidate fragments — because the TRUMPETS may be of fragments; from here: no gold — silver, iron or lead (Rebbi), even wood (R. Yehudah), never fragments; the trumpets: silver only, never gold, but fragments allowed — A 2×2 VERDICT TABLE (material / one piece) inverted between the two vessels (the exam\'s Menachot 28a-b); the lamps, tongs and snuff-dishes from the talent and of gold but not from the beaten piece (Exod 25:39); "according to the vision" — the finished tabernacle, vessels and lampstand shown; "so he made" — Moses\' nobility. The ink: "beaten" twice in 8:4 (computed), at the Torah\'s eight seats (the cherubim, the lampstand ×4, the trumpets).')
srow(62, 1, 'CREDITED', 'READ AT num_04_kehat\'s LEDGER (2026-09-09, sitting 1 — where its 4:23 arm was the subject; the export heads it "3:24", a mistyped digit, RESEARCH_LOG.md): YEARS disqualify Levites, blemishes do not — the a-fortiori from the priests refused by "this is what applies to the Levites"; the two ages RECONCILED: "from twenty-five" (8:24) TO LEARN, "from thirty" (4:23) TO SERVE (the exam\'s Chullin 24a). Its 8:24 arm CONSUMED here: the age parameter\'s two Torah settings (computed: twenty-five at 8:24 alone; thirty at the seven seats of chapter 4) — and a THIRD in the Writings, twenty (1 Chr 23:24, 23:27, 2 Chr 31:17, Ezra 3:8 — the parser reads all three), with Chronicles\' own reason in the ink: "the Levites need no longer CARRY THE TABERNACLE" (1 Chr 23:26): the burden clause lapsed, the age dropped.')
srow(63, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'FROM FIFTY HE RETURNS — TO THE GATES AND THE SONG. "He shall return from the host of the service... and serve with his brothers" (8:25-26): not from all work — he returns to closing the gates and to Gershon\'s service; Rebbi\'s arm on "serve"/"not serve"; and in Shiloh and the Temple? "thus shall you do with the Levites IN THEIR WATCHES" — from here: BEFORE THE LAND years disqualified; after it, VOICE disqualified (the singers — the exam\'s Chullin 24a); years disqualify Levites, not priests (the mirror a-fortiori refused by "with the Levites" — and not with the priests): Levites thirty to fifty, priests from two hairs. The middot\'s case law: TWO MIRROR A-FORTIORIS (I1) EACH REFUSED BY THE VERSE\'S OWN CLAUSE — the Levites\' blemishes (62:1), the priests\' years (here). "And serve with his brothers" the clause\'s one seat (computed).')

# ---- piskaot 72-77 (10:2-10): the trumpets ----
srow(72, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'TRUMPETS BESIDE THE CLOUD; TWO, NO MORE, NO LESS; BEATEN. Why the section? 9:23 "by the word of the LORD they camped and journeyed" — yet trumpets are needed: two verses, both kept (the cloud\'s word AND the priests\' blast — the exam\'s reconciliation at 84:5); "make FOR YOURSELF" — from what is yours (Moses\' silver; Abba Chanan in R. Elazar\'s name: from the congregation, by Deut 10:1 "make for yourself an ark" against Exod 25:10 "they shall make" — yours when they do not do His will); "two trumpets" — THE MINIMUM IS TWO, and not more ("two" fixes it); alike in appearance, height and beauty; מִקְשָׁה ("beaten") — a solid bar, a craftsman\'s hard work; "for calling the congregation and for the journeying of the camps" (the two offices — the clause\'s one seat, computed). The construct "two of" the parser\'s gap again (Naso\'s owed rule, 10:2 its fourth seat).')
srow(73, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'WHERE THE PRINCES GATHER; THE PRINCES ARE ADDRESSED FIRST. Both trumpets — all the congregation to the door of the tent; one — the princes: to where? By INDUCTION (I3): "blowing" is written of both — as the first to the door, so the second; the ORDER of address: the princes first — from Num 30:2 "Moses spoke to the heads of the tribes" (R. Yonathan: from Exod 34:31-32, Aaron and the princes then all Israel): "speaking" unqualified everywhere takes the one place that names the order — the princes precede, A PARADIGM FOR EVERY SPEECH; and 30:2\'s juxtaposition to 30:3 teaches that vows are annulled by experts (the exam\'s Nedarim 78a).')
srow(73, 2, 'MATERIAL', 'TEKIAH AND TERUAH ARE TWO SOUNDS; TEKIAH-TERUAH-TEKIAH; ROSH HASHANAH BY THE IDENTITY. "You shall blow a teruah" (the wailing sound) — a teruah by itself, a tekiah (the sustained sound) by itself: from 10:7 "you shall blow but not sound a teruah" the two are distinct; tekiah PRECEDES teruah ("blow a teruah"); a tekiah FOLLOWS: from 10:6 "a teruah shall they blow" — R. Yishmael son of R. Yochanan b. Beroka: from the superfluous "SECOND" (10:6), A PROTOTYPE (I3 binyan av): the tekiah second to the teruah — tekiah-teruah-tekiah; and ROSH HASHANAH: "teruah" here, "teruah" there (I2 — the identity of wording): as here tekiah-teruah-tekiah, so there; THREE teruot written for the day (Lev 23:24, 25:9, Num 29:1) → three teruot, six tekiot; which are the Torah\'s and which the scribes\' — two and one, or one and two (R. Shmuel b. Nachmani in R. Yonathan\'s name): a parameter with two settings (the exam\'s Rosh Hashanah 33b-34a). The ink: the blow-verb eight tokens and the teruah-word five in 10:3-10 (computed).')
srow(73, 3, 'MATERIAL', 'THE NORTH AND THE WEST — ONE SET OR THREE. The east and the south each get their tekiah-teruah-tekiah (10:5-6); for the north and the west — "a teruah shall they blow for their journeys": ONE set for the two together; others: three for each — a dispute on the blasts\' count, RECORDED as two settings.')
srow(74, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'THE CONVOKING WITH TWO, WITH TEKIAH ONLY. From 10:2 both offices are with the two trumpets (10:3 "with them" — as the convoking, so the journeys); but the journeys\' tekiah-teruah-tekiah is NOT the convoking\'s: "when the assembly is gathered you shall blow a tekiah and not a teruah" (10:7) — the plain sound for the assembly, the broken sound for the march.')
srow(75, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'THE PRIESTS BLOW; BLEMISHED OR WHOLE — TARFON SAW AND FORGOT, AKIVA EXPOUNDED; THE TRUMPETS NOT FOR THE GENERATIONS. "The sons of Aaron the priests shall blow" — not Israelites (10:3\'s "they" narrowed); "the priests" — whole or blemished (R. Tarfon); whole only (R. Akiva — "priests"/"priests" with Lev 3:2, I2); R. Tarfon: "I saw Shimon, my mother\'s brother, LAME in one leg, standing and blowing"; R. Akiva: on Rosh Hashanah or the Jubilee\'s Yom Kippur — the SHOFAR, not the trumpets; Tarfon: "you have not erred... TARFON SAW AND FORGOT, AKIVA EXPOUNDED OF HIMSELF AND MATCHED THE HALAKHAH" — a witnessed memory yields to a derivation that reconstructs the forgotten day (the tradition recording its own memory failure and repair, as at Shevuot 20b); "for you a statute forever" — a STATUTE, not an heirloom: all the vessels Moses made served every generation EXCEPT THE TRUMPETS (the exam\'s Menachot 28b) — the instance-scope of a vessel read off "for you".')
srow(76, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'WAR IN YOUR LAND — ATTACKING OR ATTACKED; ANY OPPRESSION; THE BLAST IS THE REMEMBRANCE. "If you go to war in your land" — whether you go out or they come; Gog and Magog (saved with no subjugation after) or all wars; R. Akiva: "against the OPPRESSOR that oppresses you" includes blast, mildew, hard labor and ships in a tempest — the fast-day trumpets (the exam\'s Mishnah Taanit 3; Taanit 14a); "you shall be remembered" — R. Akiva: if they could blow and did not, as if not remembered; Israel is remembered only for salvation.')
srow(77, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'THE DAYS OF GLADNESS; COMMUNAL OFFERINGS ONLY; THE TRUMPETS A REMEMBRANCE, NOT A VALIDATION; KINGSHIP-VERSES FROM "I AM THE LORD". "On the day of your gladness" — the Sabbaths (R. Nathan: the daily offerings); "your festivals" — the three; "your appointed times" — Rosh Hashanah and Yom Kippur; "your new moons"; over COMMUNAL peace offerings only — by context (the congregation), or Ben Azzai\'s: burnt offerings are most holy, so these peace offerings are the communal ones (I4-shaped by the neighbor); "a remembrance" — the offering stands without the blast; "I AM THE LORD YOUR GOD" — the kingship-verses (malchuyot): Lev 23:24 gives remembrance and shofar verses, this verse the third — kingship first, then remembrance, then the shofar (the exam\'s Rosh Hashanah 32a; the liturgy\'s three blessings derived on this verse); R. Nathan from Num 23:21. "The day of your gladness" the clause\'s one seat (computed).')

# ---- piskaot 78-84 (10:29-36): Hobab, the ark, the clouds, the signs ----
srow(78, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'HOBAB OR REUEL — THE FATHER\'S FATHER CALLED FATHER; SEVEN NAMES; THE PROSELYTE DRAWN NEAR. Was Hobab the father-in-law, or Reuel (Exod 2:18 "they came to Reuel their father")? Judg 4:11 "the children of Hobab, the father-in-law of Moses" decides: HOBAB; "Reuel their father" — children call the grandfather father (the ink: "Hobab" at Judg 4:11 and here; "Reuel" at 2:14 for Deuel and at Exod 2:18, 10:29 for Jethro\'s house — computed); the names expounded — Reuel (friend of God), Keini (separated from the provokers; acquired Torah), Hobab (loved the Torah), Yithro (added a section — Exod 18:21\'s judges: "were these not known to Moses from Sinai? — to credit Jethro"); his descendants the scribes of Jabez (1 Chr 2:55, Tirathim/Shimathim/Suchathim expounded), the Rechabites (Jer 35) in the Sanhedrin; THE A-FORTIORI OF THE DRAWN-NEAR (I1): if the proselytes who drew near were drawn near, how much more Israel who do His will — Rahab (eight prophets and Huldah), the Gibeonites, Ruth (Yoash and Saraph = Mahlon and Chilion; "the king\'s mother" 1 Kgs 2:19 = Ruth), the midwives (Shifra = Jochebed, Puah = Miriam; "houses" = priesthood and royalty). The identification and the names are RECORDED as the shelf\'s; the a-fortiori\'s form is the claim.')
srow(78, 2, 'CONTEXT', 'CALEB\'S NAMES AND MIRIAM\'S (1 Chr 4:5-8 expounded name by name: Ashchur = Caleb; Helah and Naarah, Zereth, Zohar, Ethnan, Aharhel, Harum = Miriam and her line) — David from Miriam\'s descendants; "one who draws near is drawn near". Genealogical expansion on the Writings, not this span\'s verse.')
srow(78, 3, 'MATERIAL', 'THE HIGHEST TRIBUTE; "WE ARE JOURNEYING" — WHY MOSES INCLUDED HIMSELF; NO PORTION FOR PROSELYTES; GOOD TO THE STRANGER COMMANDED. "The father-in-law of Moses" — the highest title; "we are journeying" (the clause\'s one seat, computed) — R. Shimon b. Yochai: Deut 4:22 "I shall not cross" — even his bones; why "we"? so Israel not say "if he does not enter, neither we"; or so Jethro not say it; the sages: he lost sight of it; "to you" — proselytes have NO PORTION in the land (Ezek 47:23\'s portion read as atonement with the tribe, or burial); "we will do good with you" — the a-fortiori (I1) from a household\'s member to the Lord\'s; "the LORD has spoken good for Israel" — the command to do good to proselytes. Three readings of one pronoun RECORDED.')
srow(79, 1, 'CONTEXT', 'JETHRO\'S THREE REASONS: land, possessions, family — "I was a priest in my land"; if not for one, then for the next. The refusal\'s ladder, the shelf\'s gloss on 10:30.')
srow(80, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'THE ROW ON 10:31 (headed "10:30" in the export; placed between 79 on 10:30 and 81 on 10:32 by its opening "do not leave us"): "na" is IMPLORATION (the lexical rule, stated again at 103:1); Moses\' decree — if you leave, Israel will say Jethro converted for a portion; "you diminish God\'s honor" — the proselytes you would shelter; "you know our camping" — one who saw the miracles cannot leave (R. Yehudah: "the FAVOR" — chanotenu read as chen, Exod 12:36); "you shall be eyes for us" (the clause\'s one seat, computed) — the judges credited to Jethro again; or: the stranger as beloved as the eye (Deut 10:19; Exod 22:20). Onkelos\' insertion at this verse — "the mighty deeds done for us you SAW with your eyes" — is this row\'s reading (the spine agrees with itself).')
srow(81, 1, 'CONTEXT', 'THE GOOD ACCORDED: the choicest of Jericho, five hundred by five hundred cubits, held by Jethro\'s sons until the Temple\'s builder took it — "four hundred and forty years" (the export writes 1 Kgs 6:1 as "the four hundred and EIGHTEENTH year"; the ink says 480 — the parser reads [480] on 1 Kgs 6:1 — and the row\'s own arithmetic, "deduct forty", fits 480: the export\'s numeral mistyped, recorded); vacated when the Shekhinah rested in Benjamin\'s portion.')
srow(82, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'THREE DAYS IN ONE DAY; THE ARK OF THE BROKEN TABLETS; THE SPYING VERB. "A journey of three days" against Deut 1:2\'s eleven from Horeb: they went a three-day journey IN ONE DAY, the Shekhinah before them to bring them in at once; "the ark of the covenant of the LORD went before them" — the ark of the BROKEN TABLETS (14:44\'s ark stays in the camp); R. Shimon b. Yochai: "the covenant\'s ark" — the viceroy preparing the camp = the Shekhinah; "to seek out a resting place" → Num 21:1 (Arad heard the lookout was gone); RSBY: the spies\' request (Deut 1:22) a degradation — "I looked out the way for you". THE INK\'S OWN VERB: לָתוּר ("to spy out", 10:33) is the SPIES\' verb of chapters 13-14 (six seats) and Deut 1:33\'s "to seek you out a place" — the ark spies before the men do (computed); "a journey of three days" twice in the verse, at seven Torah tokens (computed).')
srow(83, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'SEVEN CLOUDS — OR THIRTEEN, FOUR, TWO. From seven verses (Num 14:14 twice, Exod 14:19, Deut 1:33, Num 9:19, Exod 40:38, Num 10:34) SEVEN clouds: four sides, above, below, and one before that leveled the way, killed serpents and scorpions, swept and sprinkled; R. Yehudah: thirteen; R. Yoshiyah: four; Rebbi: two — A PARAMETER WITH FOUR SETTINGS (7/13/4/2), the count of the clouds, RECORDED. The ink: "the cloud of the LORD" at its two seats, Exod 40:38 and 10:34 (computed) — the list\'s two.')
srow(83, 2, 'CONTEXT', 'THE CLOUD OVER ALL — the lame, the blind, the zavim (those with a discharge), the lepers: no one outside it.')
srow(83, 3, 'CONTEXT', 'BY DAY, NOT BY NIGHT; THE FIRE FOR ISRAEL, NOT THE NATIONS; A TORCH IN THE INNER ROOM. One who withdrew from the cloud — it withdrew with him until he returned; "by day" excludes the night (Exod 40:38 the fire by night, "in the sight of all the house of Israel"); R. Shimon b. Elazar: forty years without a lamp.')
srow(84, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'THE SIGNS — A BOOK IN ITSELF, OR NOT ITS PLACE. "And it was when the ark journeyed": SIGNS before and after (the inverted nuns — the Tanakh DB carries them as marks after 10:34 and after 10:36; nine in the Bible with Psalm 107\'s seven; the snapshot store none — computed); Rebbi: A BOOK IN ITSELF — whence: a scroll erased with EIGHTY-FIVE letters left, as this section, defiles the hands (the exam\'s Shabbat 115b-116a; Mishnah Yadayim 3:5) — AND THE INK PROVES THE NUMBER: 10:35-36 have exactly 85 letters (computed); R. Shimon: not its place — it belongs after 10:33 before 11:1\'s complaint (the governor of Acco: the king put to trouble for their sakes complains, not they).')
srow(84, 2, 'MATERIAL', 'TWO VERSES RECONCILED BY A MODEL. "Moses said: Rise, LORD" against 9:23 "by the word of the LORD they camped and journeyed" — reconciled by an analogy (the king: "stop me"; the king and his lover: "I will not move before you tell me") — a reconciliation of two verses WITHOUT a third (beside I13\'s form; MIDDOT.md).')
srow(84, 3, 'CONTEXT', '"YOUR FOES" — those massed against us; "before Your face" — when Your face is with us we do not flee (Exod 33:15-16; Josh 10:11; Ps 83:14). Onkelos renders "Rise" as "REVEAL YOURSELF" (cut from the shelf\'s bytes).')
srow(84, 4, 'MATERIAL', 'THE HATERS OF THE RIGHTEOUS ARE HIS HATERS; SCRIPTURE\'S EUPHEMISMS INCLUDE 11:15 AND 12:12. "Your haters" — those who hate the righteous, as it were (Exod 15:7; Ps 74:23, 83:3-4, 139:21-22); "the pupil of HIS eye" (Zech 2:12) — SCRIPTURE\'S EUPHEMISM (kinah hakatuv), and the list: Job 7:20 ("to myself" for "to You"), Ezek 8:17, Hab 1:12, Ps 106:20, AND THIS PORTION\'S TWO — Num 11:15 "let me not see MY evil" (for "their"), Num 12:12 "HIS mother\'s womb... half HIS flesh" (for "our"): the reading tradition\'s record of the ink\'s transmitted euphemisms at two of the span\'s verses (the ink writes בְּרָעָתִי "in my evil" — the form "your evil" exists at 2 Sam 16:8, Isa 47:10 — computed); the Shekhinah in every exile and returning "WITH your captivity" (Deut 30:3 — ושב "and He will return", not "bring back"); Pharaoh, Sisera, Sennacherib, Nebuchadnezzar, Haman; Isa 63:9. The euphemism-claim is the tradition\'s about the ink; RECORDED as such.')
srow(84, 5, 'MATERIAL', 'THE CLOUD FOLDED UNTIL MOSES SPOKE; "BY THE MOUTH OF THE LORD BY THE HAND OF MOSES"; THE SHEKHINAH ON TWENTY-TWO THOUSAND. Rebbi\'s reconciliation of 9:23 and 10:35-36: the cloud folded and stood until Moses said "Rise", spread until "Rest" — both verses satisfied; and THIS is "by the mouth of the LORD by the hand of Moses" (the formula at 4:37, 4:45, 9:23, 10:13 — and Josh 22:9; computed — the run-citation the compile\'s dependency gate reads); 10:36 "Rest, LORD, among the myriads of the thousands of Israel": Moses would not let the Shekhinah rest until Israel were thousands and myriads; the Shekhinah rests only on TWO THOUSANDS AND TWO MYRIADS (Ps 68:18 "the chariots of God are two myriads, thousands upon thousands") = 22,000 — the shelf reads the two plural nouns as DUALS, a number the parser leaves silent (10:36 → [], computed; the exam\'s Yevamot 64a) and the number of the Levites (3:39\'s 22,000 — the Bamidbar cell).')

# ---- piskaot 85-98 (11:1-35): Taberah, the lust, the elders, the quail ----
srow(85, 1, 'MATERIAL', '"THE PEOPLE" ARE THE WICKED; GRUMBLERS SEEKING A PRETEXT; THEY MEANT HIM TO HEAR; THE FIRE AT THE EDGE. "And it was" — a return to a former state; "THE PEOPLE" everywhere the wicked (Exod 17:4; Num 14:11; Jer 13:10), "MY PEOPLE" the upright (Exod 7:16; Mic 6:3, 6:5) — a lexical rule with proof-seats; מִתְאֹנְנִים ("murmurers", the word\'s one seat — computed) — seekers of a pretext (2 Kgs 5:7; Judg 14:4); R. Eliezer: "blows" (Prov 26:22); R. Yehudah: self-affliction (Deut 26:14); Rebbi: "evil" = idolatry; "in the ears of the LORD" — they intended Him to hear (the cursing man and the passing king); the fire rained blows — the living not told from the dead; "the edge of the camp" — the proselytes cast to the edge, or the officers (R. Shimon b. Menassia). "The fire of the LORD" at 11:1, 11:3 and Elijah\'s 1 Kgs 18:38 (computed).')
srow(86, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'THE INTERCESSOR; THE FIRE SANK IN ITS PLACE; NAMES BY THE EVENT; THE RABBLE — PROSELYTES OR ELDERS; THEY HAD FLOCKS. "Cried to Moses" — the king\'s loved one asked to intercede; "Moses prayed"; "the fire SANK" (וַתִּשְׁקַע, the verb\'s one seat in the Torah — computed) — in its place: not to heaven (they would revert), not sideways (it would raze); TABERAH named FOR THE EVENT, not before — as Massah-Meribah (Exod 17:7) and Kibroth-hattaavah (11:34): a naming rule read off "because" (three seats); THE ASAFSUF (the word\'s one seat) — the proselytes "added on", or the ELDERS (R. Shimon b. Menassia — from "gather", 11:16) — either way the a-fortiori (I1) to the commoners; "lusted a lust" — a thing they HAD ("who will feed us flesh" — Exod 12:38\'s flocks, Num 32:1\'s cattle): a pretext; "ALSO the children of Israel wept AGAIN" — the first weepers were Israel.')
srow(87, 1, 'MATERIAL', '"FREE" — FREE OF COMMANDMENTS; THE MANNA TOOK EVERY TASTE BUT FIVE. Fish free in Egypt? — no straw was free (Exod 5:18): free of MITZVOT; R. Shimon: the manna changed to every taste EXCEPT the five named (cucumbers, melons, leeks, onions, garlic — harmful to a nursling: the pedagogue\'s charge); the sages: every taste, but not seen — "nothing before our eyes but the manna". The five foods: four words at one seat each in the Bible, and "leeks" a homograph of "grass" (computed).')
srow(88, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'THE MANNA NEVER EXPELLED; THE SPLIT REFERENT — ONE VERSE, TWO SPEAKERS, SEVEN PARALLELS. "It will burst our bowels" — R. Shimon: the manna absorbed in the limbs (Ps 78:25 "bread of the mighty"); the spade (Deut 23:14) for the merchants\' food; "only to the manna are our eyes" is ISRAEL\'S, and "the manna was like coriander seed, like crystal" (11:7) is GOD\'S ANSWER to the generations — a clause-attribution rule with parallels: Gen 38:25-26 (Judah / Scripture), Deut 25:18 (Israel faint / Amalek unfearing), Judg 5:28-31 (Sisera\'s mother / her ladies / Deborah), 1 Sam 4:8 (the righteous / the wicked), Jer 26:16-24, Ruth 3:13 (Boaz to his inclination / to Ruth) — THE SPEAKER SPLIT (a move candidate: adjacent clauses of one verse assigned to two voices by the teacher; MOVE_CATALOG). The ink: "coriander seed" at Exod 16:31 and here; "bdellium" at Gen 2:12 and here (computed).')
srow(89, 1, 'CONTEXT', 'THE MANNA CONVERTED TO EVERYTHING GROUND, BEATEN, COOKED, BAKED AND GATHERED; LESHAD AS AN ACRONYM; THE BREAST; DAILY FOR THE HEART. "They strolled and gathered" — at the door, before the sun; the mill, the mortar, the pot, the oven — "it never descended to them": it was CONVERTED to their products; a woman perfumed by it; Deut 2:7 "you lacked nothing"; לְשַׁד ("moist cake") = dough, oil, honey (E30 notarikon); the breast\'s five likenesses; Josh 5:12 the manna ceased; the dew above and below (Exod 16:14) — the Shema and prayer first; daily so hearts turn to their Father (R. Shimon), warm and light (R. Dostai); Tiberias\' springs. The homilies RECORDED; the ink\'s two tastes computed (Exod 16:31\'s honey wafer; 11:8\'s oil cake — one seat each).')
srow(90, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'WEEPING BY FAMILIES — OVER THE FAMILIES\' MARRIAGES; GOD ATTENUATES, MOSES EXACERBATES. R. Nehorai: "weeping by its families" (the clause\'s one seat — computed) — Israel grieved when charged to abstain from the forbidden relations (a man had married his sister or aunt) — the families weep for the family law (the exam\'s Yoma 75a; Shabbat 130a); "at the door of his tent" — waiting for Moses to leave the study house (the tent-door standing of Exod 33:8-10 — computed); "the LORD\'s anger burned greatly and in Moses\' eyes it was evil" — here God attenuates and Moses exacerbates; at the calf the reverse.')
srow(91, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'WHEN THE BURDEN WAS LAID; KILL ME FIRST. "Why have You dealt ill" (הֲרֵעֹתָ, "You have dealt ill" — Moses at Exod 5:22 and here, Elijah at 1 Kgs 17:20: three forms, three seats — computed): when? Exod 32:34 "lead the people" and Exod 6:13 "He charged them... to bring out" — on the understanding they will curse and stone you; "one or two?" — the majority; "kill me, I pray" — He had shown Moses the calamity: R. Shimon\'s executioner — kill me before my sons (not Zedekiah\'s fate, Jer 52:10-11). "Kill me, kill" the cognate\'s one seat; "my evil" the euphemism of 84:4 (computed).')
srow(92, 1, 'MATERIAL', '"UNTO ME" IS FOREVER — TEN SEATS; SEVENTY IN A SANHEDRIN; THE ELDERS HONORED AT EVERY SEAT. "Gather unto Me seventy men" — the Sanhedrin in My name; "UNTO ME" everywhere = FOREVER: the priests (Exod 28:41), the Levites (Num 8:14), Israel (Lev 25:55), the firstborn (Num 8:17), the sanctuary (Exod 25:8), the altar (Exod 20:24), the anointing oil (Exod 30:31), the kings (1 Sam 16:1), the offerings (Num 28:2) — a lexical rule with TEN proof-seats, EVERY ONE ON THE INK (computed: "unto Me" at all ten); "seventy" — a Sanhedrin\'s number (the exam\'s Mishnah Sanhedrin 1:6 — seventy-one with Moses); wise, strong, senior, versed in the arts; "the elders" honored at every seat (Exod 3:16, 24:1, 24:14; Lev 9:1; Isa 24:23) — the a-fortiori (I1) to flesh and blood; "whom you know" — select; chosen by public praise; "its officers" — the officers beaten in Egypt (Exod 5:14) share the honor; "take them" — with words, praise then hard words; "stand there with you" — in awe. "Seventy men" at 11:16, 11:24, 11:25; "and seventy of the elders of Israel" at Exod 24:1, 24:9 (computed).')
srow(93, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'ONE OF THE TEN DESCENTS; WITH YOU, NOT WITH THEM; THE LAMP THAT LIGHTS LAMPS. "I will come down" — one of the TEN descents written in the Torah (the shelf\'s count; the ink carries ELEVEN tokens of the LORD going down — Gen 11:5, 11:7, 18:21; Exod 3:8, 19:11, 19:18, 19:20, 34:5; Num 11:17, 11:25, 12:5 — computed; the shelf\'s list of ten is not on this shelf: DIVERGE by one, recorded); "and I will speak WITH YOU" — not with them; "I will increase of the spirit upon you" — Moses a lamp on the lampstand: many lit, none of his light lost (Onkelos "I will make greater" agrees); "they will bear with you" — Deut 1:12\'s burden.')
srow(94, 1, 'MATERIAL', '"PREPARE" IS FOR CALAMITY; A MONTH FOR THE MEDIOCRE, THE TEETH FOR THE WICKED; THE SHEKHINAH THE CAUSE OF THEIR PRIDE. "Sanctify yourselves for tomorrow" — prepare for calamity (Jer 12:3, 22:7); "until a month of days" — the MEDIOCRE languished thirty days; the wicked died with the flesh between their teeth (11:33): ONE PLAGUE, TWO TIMERS BY DESERT (0 days / 30 days) — a verdict table on the same act; "loathsome" — repelled more than courted; "you despised the LORD in your midst" — My Shekhinah among you made you bold. The ink\'s ladder 11:19-20 — one day, two days, five, ten, twenty, a month (computed; "two days" a dual the parser leaves silent).')
srow(95, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'AKIVA PLAIN, SHIMON TWO WAYS; THE FLOCKS AND THE WELL\'S FISH; GIVE AND KILL? "Six hundred thousand on foot" (the phrase\'s two seats — Exod 12:37 "ABOUT six hundred thousand", here without the "about" — computed): R. Akiva expounds "will flocks suffice" plainly; R. Shimon b. Yochai two ways — they had flocks (Exod 12:38; Num 32:1) and Miriam\'s well gave fish: A PRETEXT; and: "is it right to give and kill?" (the ass and the kor; the loaf and Sheol) — "if not, what will they say? Will the LORD\'s hand be short?" (the hand\'s three seats — Isa 50:2, 59:1 — computed); Moses went to conciliate; the people: "He struck a rock... but can He give bread?" (Ps 78:20) — "a compromise".')
srow(95, 2, 'MATERIAL', 'THE LOTS — SEVENTY-TWO BALLOTS, TWO BLANK; THE SAME MACHINE FOR THE 273 FIRSTBORN; ELDAD AND MEDAD EXALTED. "Two men remained in the camp" — their ballots remained in the box: six per tribe is seventy-two, so seventy marked "elder" and two blank (which tribe consents to five?); "the LORD has chosen you" / "it is Heaven\'s will"; and for the 273 firstborn over the Levites (3:46) — 22,000 ballots "Levite" and 273 "five shekels": THE LOT IS THE SELECTION MECHANISM of the redemption cell (Bamidbar\'s compiled excess, chosen by lot — the exam\'s Sanhedrin 17a); R. Shimon: they hid ("we are not worthy") and were exalted — the seventy "prophesied and did not continue", Eldad and Medad prophesied until their death: "Moses dies and Joshua brings Israel in". Two readings of "remained" RECORDED; "among the written" the word\'s one seat (computed).')
srow(96, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'THE YOUTH; "RESTRAIN THEM" — END THEM OR CONFINE THEM; WOULD THAT ALL WERE PROPHETS. "The youth ran" — Joshua (Exod 33:11), or not (R. Shimon: 11:28 names Joshua separately — the ink\'s "the youth" is Numbers\' one such token, computed); "kela\'em" — end them from the world (the report "Moses dies"), or confine them in chains (Rebbi, Jer 37:18) — two readings of the verb, Onkelos "BIND them" with Rebbi (cut from the shelf\'s bytes); "are you zealous for me?" — would that you were a prophet like me and all Israel like you: by direct inspiration, not by the increase of spirit; Moses retired with the elders — the calamity waited until the righteous were in.')
srow(97, 1, 'CONTEXT', 'THE QUAIL "BLOSSOMED" LIKE WOOL; A DAY\'S JOURNEY NORTH AND SOUTH (R. Shimon: above and below); TWO CUBITS — hovering, for easy gathering. The ink: וַיָּגָז ("and it blew in") the Torah\'s one seat; "about two cubits" the dual at the ark\'s and table\'s seven seats and here (computed; the parser silent on the dual).')
srow(98, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'THE LEAST GATHERED TEN; SLAUGHTERED, OR IN LAYERS; THE FLESH BETWEEN THE TEETH; NAMED FOR THE EVENT; TWO HAZEROTHS — A RETREAT. "He who gathered least" read "the least among them" (the lame, the indolent) — ten kor (the homer as the kor: the shelf\'s conversion; "ten homers" the same consonants as Joseph\'s "ten asses" at Gen 45:23 — computed); "they spread them a spreading" read "they SLAUGHTERED" (R. Yehudah: the quail needed slaughter — the exam\'s Chullin 27b) or "in layers" (Rebbi, Ps 78:27); "the flesh yet between their teeth" (Ps 78:30-31); a plague unseen since Egypt; KIBROTH-HATTAAVAH named for the event; "from Kibroth-hattaavah to Hazeroth, and they were in Hazeroth" — TWO HAZEROTHS? they set out, heard of Miriam, and turned back to camp — hence 12:16 "afterwards they journeyed from Hazeroth": the doubled place read as a retreat (the ink: Hazeroth twice in 11:35, plene in the story and DEFECTIVE in the itinerary 33:17-18 and Deut 1:1; the graves of lust plene at 11:34-35, defective at 33:16-17 and Deut 9:22 — computed).')

# ---- piskaot 99-106 (12:1-16): Miriam ----
srow(99, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'DIBBUR IS HARSH, AMIRAH IMPLORES; MIRIAM SPOKE FIRST; HOW SHE KNEW; THE A-FORTIORI OF SLANDER; CUSHITE = EXCEPTIONAL; BEAUTIFUL IN LOOKS AND DEEDS. "Spoke" (dibbur) everywhere is harsh (Gen 42:30; Num 21:5), "said" (amirah) imploring (Gen 19:7; Num 12:6) — a lexical rule with proof-seats; "and Miriam spoke, and Aaron" — MIRIAM SPOKE FIRST (the ink: וַתְּדַבֵּר, the feminine singular verb before two subjects — computed; Baruch before Jeremiah, Jer 36:6); how she knew — Zipporah unadorned: "your brother is not particular about this"; THE A-FORTIORI (I1): Miriam meant praise, increase and privacy and was punished — how much more one who defames, diminishes, in public (the exam\'s Arakhin 15a-16b; Deut 24:9); Uzziah\'s a-fortiori; "the Cushite woman" — all attested her beauty (Iscah = Sarah; Zipporah = "look and see"); CUSHITE = EXCEPTIONAL as a Cushite in his skin (Saul Ps 7:1; Israel Amos 9:7; Baruch = Ebed-melech Jer 38:7) — a lexical rule; "about the Cushite woman... for he had taken a Cushite woman" — beautiful in appearance AND in deed (Prov 11:22). Onkelos renders both as "the BEAUTIFUL woman" and adds "he had DISTANCED" (cut from the shelf\'s bytes) — the spine agrees with itself twice on this verse.')
srow(100, 1, 'MATERIAL', '"ONLY WITH MOSES?" — THE FOREFATHERS AND WE DID NOT SEPARATE; NO ONE ELSE HEARD. "Has the LORD spoken only with Moses? — and not with our forefathers, who did not separate from their wives? — also with us, who did not separate"; "and the LORD heard" — no one else was there; R. Nathan: to Moses\' face too — "and the man Moses" — but Moses suppressed it. The ink: "and the LORD heard" opens both punishments of the portion, 11:1 and 12:2 (computed); the doubled restrictive (הֲרַק אַךְ, "is it only, only") at 12:2.')
srow(101, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'HUMBLE IN MIND, NOT IN WEALTH; THE SAPPHIRE TABLETS BY THE IDENTITY "WORK"; NOT MORE THAN THE FOREFATHERS. "Humble" — in mind; not in wealth (Exod 11:3 "the man Moses was very great"): the second tablets of sapphire (Deut 10:1 "carve for yourself" — the chips his), the first of sapphire by "work"/"work" (Exod 32:16 / 24:10 — I2); "more than any man on the face of the earth" — not than the forefathers (R. Yossi: even them; not than the angels). THE INK: "humble" WRITTEN עָנָו (without the yod) AND READ עָנָיו — the portion\'s one written-and-read pair (the Tanakh DB\'s one unpointed token with its note; the snapshot store carries both tokens side by side, as at 1:16 — computed).')
srow(102, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'THE ROW ON 12:4 (headed "Ibid. 4" in the export; by position between 101 on 12:3 and 103 on 12:6): "suddenly" — Moses feared it (Exod 3:6), God spoke it; "you three, come out" — the three called BY ONE UTTERANCE (what the mouth cannot say nor the ear hear — Exod 20:1; Ps 62:12; Jer 23:29); "the LORD came down in a pillar of cloud" — not as flesh and blood: to war alone (Exod 15:3), to peace with myriads (Ps 68:18); "He called Aaron and Miriam" — draw the one near, do not send the other away (proper conduct); why not Moses — so Israel not think him rebuked; so he not hear Aaron\'s; A MAN IS NOT PRAISED TO HIS FACE — R. Elazar b. Azaryah: PART of his praise to his face — Noah 7:1 "righteous" to his face against 6:9 "righteous, whole" behind him; R. Elazar son of R. Yossi HaGelili: even of God only part to His face (Ps 66:3). THE STANDING SEAT: the Genesis unit read exactly this off the 6:9/7:1 ink-delta (gen_16_ark_spec G16-18 — CREDITED, the Sifrei\'s own statement of the seated rule). The ink: "the three of you" and "the three of them" each one seat; the summons "Aaron and Miriam" reverses 12:1\'s "Miriam and Aaron"; "suddenly" at three Torah seats (computed).')
srow(103, 1, 'MATERIAL', '"NA" IMPLORES — THE A-FORTIORI OF CONDUCT; DO NOT INTERRUPT; VISION AND DREAM FOR PROPHETS, MOUTH TO MOUTH FOR MOSES; NO MAN SEES AND LIVES; THE BACK, NOT THE FACE. "Hear, I pray, My words" — if He implores His creatures, how much more flesh and blood (I1); R. Shimon b. Yochai: they tried to enter His words — wait till He finishes; "in a vision I make Myself known, in a dream I speak" — but not so Moses: "in all My house faithful" — above the angels (R. Yossi); "MOUTH TO MOUTH" (the phrase\'s one seat — computed) — I told him to separate from his wife; "in a vision" — of His WORDS, not the Shekhinah: Exod 33:20 "no man shall see Me and live" — R. Akiva: "and live" = the living ones, the angels; R. Shimon: the holy creatures; R. Elazar son of R. Yossi: they do not know where it is (Ezek 3:12); R. Dossa: he sees at death (Ps 22:30); "not in riddles" — Ezek 17:2\'s riddle to the prophets (the riddle-word\'s one Torah seat — computed); "the likeness of the LORD he beholds" — His BACK (Exod 33:23): face and back = this world and the world to come (Ezek 2:10\'s scroll; kinim, hegeh, hi); "against My servant, against Moses" — against Me. THE INK: the likeness no one may make (seven bans, Exod 20:4; Deut 4:12-25, 5:8) is what Moses looks at (12:8 — the word\'s eighth Torah seat, computed).')
srow(104, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'HE TOLD THEM THEIR OFFENSE, THEN DEPARTED — THE A-FORTIORI OF ANGER. "The LORD\'s anger burned against them and He went" — after He apprised them He decreed ostracism: if He did not vent wrath until He told them, how much more flesh and blood (I1); R. Nathan: so they not say as Job (10:2). The ink: the portion\'s four anger clauses (11:1, 11:10, 11:33, 12:9 — computed); "against THEM" plural (the exam\'s Shabbat 97a: Aaron too).')
srow(105, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'THE CLOUD LEFT FIRST; LEPROUS AS SNOW; AARON TURNED — FROM HIS OWN; THE COVERED THREE; A PRIEST DOES NOT INSPECT HIS KIN; THE EUPHEMISMS; THE SHORTEST PRAYER. "The cloud departed" — the pedagogue chastises after the father leaves (a father\'s mercy; Isa 49:8); "leprous as snow" — intense, on fair skin (Exod 4:6\'s hand; the phrase\'s three seats with Gehazi\'s — computed); "Aaron TURNED" — was turned FROM HIS leprosy; R. Yehudah b. Beteira: who says Aaron was stricken will pay; WHO SAYS ZELOPHEHAD WAS THE WOOD-GATHERER WILL PAY (against R. Akiva at Sifrei 113:1 — the tent\'s num_15 unit carries the dispute unresolved: NM15-01); who says Akavya was banned will pay — Scripture covered them; "whenever he looked she was leprous"; "as one dead" — the leper defiles by entry as the corpse by tent (I3); "our sister loses on all accounts: I cannot quarantine, declare unclean or clean" — A PRIEST DOES NOT INSPECT HIS KIN (the exam\'s Zevachim 101b-102a; Mishnah Negaim 2:5); "his mother", "his flesh" — Scripture\'s euphemisms for "our" (84:4); "El na refa na lah" — two or three words of imploration before a request; "saying" = answer me (the four places Moses asked and was answered — Exod 6:12, Num 27:15, Deut 3:23, and here); why so short — Israel not say "his sister in distress and he prolongs"; or the righteous decree (Job 22:28); R. Eliezer: not longer than forty days (Deut 9:18), not shorter than this (the exam\'s Berakhot 34a). The ink: FIVE WORDS, ELEVEN LETTERS (computed); Moses\' four cries to the LORD (Exod 8:8, 15:25, 17:4; here).')
srow(106, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'DAYO — THE A-FORTIORI\'S CAP STATED ON ITS VERSE; GOD QUARANTINED HER; MEASURE FOR MEASURE; THE BURIALS. "If her father had spat in her face, would she not be ashamed seven days?" — R. Achi b. R. Yoshiyah: two rebukes — the father\'s seven, so His FOURTEEN — BUT "IT SUFFICES THAT WHAT IS DERIVED FROM AN A-FORTIORI BE AS THAT FROM WHICH IT IS DERIVED" (dayo): seven — THE MIDDOT\'S OWN CASE LAW ON I1\'S CEILING, stated on its home verse (the exam\'s Bava Kamma 25a; Mishnah Bava Kamma 2:5; MIDDOT.md); the Holy One quarantined her, declared her unclean, declared her clean (the quarantine verb of Lev 13-14\'s nine seats at Miriam\'s two — computed; Onkelos renders the spitting as REBUKING, cut from the shelf\'s bytes); "the people did not journey until Miriam was gathered in" — WITH THE MEASURE A MAN MEASURES: Miriam waited a short while for Moses (Exod 2:4), so the Shekhinah, the ark, the priests, the Levites and the seven clouds waited seven days — Mishnah Sotah 1:9\'s row on this verse (E27 symmetry); Joseph buried Jacob, Moses buried Joseph, the Holy One buried Moses — in Gad\'s portion though he died in Reuben\'s (Deut 34:1, 33:20-21; Num 32:37-38), four mils in His hand; "afterwards the people journeyed" — after Miriam.')

assert len(S) == 51 and sorted(S) == sorted((p, r) for p in PISKAOT for r in range(1, SIF_ROWS[p] + 1)), (len(S), sorted(S)[:5])
